# What must not enter the build context.
#
# Three reasons a line appears here: it is a secret that must never exist in an image
# layer (layers are readable by anyone who can pull the image, and deleting a file in a
# later layer does not remove it from the earlier one); it is generated data that belongs
# in a volume rather than in an image; or it is large and would be copied on every build.
#
# The exclusions mirror .gitignore rather than relying on re-inclusion patterns, so that
# data/controls/control_library.json - which the startup seeding genuinely needs - is
# simply never excluded in the first place.

# ---- secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# ---- local virtualenv ----------------------------------------------------
# macOS/CPython 3.9 binaries: useless inside a Linux 3.12 image, and hundreds of MB.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ---- version control -----------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitattributes
.github/

# ---- generated runtime data ----------------------------------------------
# The database, uploaded evidence and generated reports live in a volume. Baking a
# database into an image would also ship whatever evidence the author had loaded.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
data/uploads/*
data/reports/*
data/evaluation/*
data/synthetic/*
data/sample_evidence/*
logs/
*.log

# ---- caches --------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# ---- editors and OS ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
